  "body": "Recently I've been delving into PWAs and building responsive, mobile first websites. My issue is that when it comes to keyboard input for soft keyboard on mobile it seems the web has no good way of doing basic things. For example programmatically dismissing the keyboard. Or more simple things like adding event listeners for keyboard open and keyboard close. I propose a Keyboard API/Soft Keyboard API to do just that and give PWA developers more flexibility when it comes to soft keyboard inputs. I think the [react native keyboard API](https://reactnative.dev/docs/keyboard) gives a good baseline for what I'm going for. ",
